     be released using ggeeoomm__ddeelleetteettrreeee() after use.

     The ggeeoomm__ddeelleetteettrreeee() function releases memory allocated for storing the
     data-structures referenced by _g_m_p.

     The gg__**() functions are used to communicate with GEOM providers.

     The gg__ooppeenn() function opens the given provider and returns file descrip‐
     tor number, which can be used with other functions.  The _d_o_w_r_i_t_e argument
     indicates if operations that modify the provider (like gg__fflluusshh() or
     gg__ddeelleettee()) are going to be called.

     The gg__cclloossee() function closes the provider.

     The gg__mmeeddiiaassiizzee() function returns size of the given provider.

     The gg__sseeccttoorrssiizzee() function returns sector size of the given provider.

     The gg__ssttrriippeeooffffsseett() function returns stripe offset of the given
     provider.

     The gg__ssttrriippeessiizzee() function returns stripe size of the given provider.

     The gg__fflluusshh() function sends BIO_FLUSH request to flush write cache of
     the provider.

     The gg__ddeelleettee() function tells the provider that the given data range is
     no longer used.

     The gg__ddeevviiccee__ppaatthh() function returns the full path to a provider given a
     partial or full path to the device node.  NULL is returned if the device
